From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] addons: update the add-ons YBLOD pre-installs from its own
 repository

The optional system add-ons YBLOD pre-installs from
repository.dangerouslaser (Estuary YBLOD, the LG edition's webOS add-on
and the repository add-on itself) keep the system origin, so Kodi only
ever looked for their updates in the official repositories, where they
are not.

Look for their updates in that repository's entries of
m_latestVersionsByRepo, and only there (keyed by the repository's id,
which is the origin of each remote add-on; disabled repositories are
not loaded). Taking them from any installed repository would bypass the
origin pinning that protects system add-ons: any repository a user
installed could replace them. As for an add-on installed from a
third-party repository, which always updates from its origin
repository, the "update official add-ons from" mode is not consulted:
it defaults to official repositories only, so honouring it would stop
these add-ons from ever updating. The automatic-update setting and
per-add-on update rules still apply downstream (CRepositoryUpdater,
CAddonMgr::GetAddonUpdateCandidates).

Applies to Kodi as LibreELEC patches it; needs nothing else from this
series. Formerly yblod-20 (optional system add-ons take updates) and
yblod-53 (from repository.dangerouslaser only).
---
 xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp b/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp
index 1172b3e..43f838c 100644
--- a/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/addons/AddonRepos.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ namespace
 {
 constexpr auto ALL_ADDON_IDS = "";
 constexpr auto ALL_REPOSITORIES = nullptr;
+// The repository that updates the optional system add-ons YBLOD pre-installs.
+constexpr auto YBLOD_REPOSITORY = "repository.dangerouslaser";
 } // anonymous namespace
 
 using namespace ADDON;
@@ -262,6 +264,18 @@ bool CAddonRepos::DoAddonUpdateCheck(const std::shared_ptr<IAddon>& addon,
       }
     }
   }
+  // YBLOD: the optional system add-ons YBLOD pre-installs from its own repository (Estuary
+  // YBLOD, the LG edition's webOS add-on and the repository itself) keep the system origin, so
+  // they would only ever be updated from the official repositories. Take their updates from that
+  // repository and no other: like an add-on installed from a third-party repository, which
+  // updates from its origin repository whatever the update mode.
+  else if (addon->Origin() == ORIGIN_SYSTEM && !hasOfficialUpdate &&
+           CServiceBroker::GetAddonMgr().IsOptionalSystemAddon(addon->ID()))
+  {
+    const auto repoEntryIt = m_latestVersionsByRepo.find(YBLOD_REPOSITORY);
+    if (repoEntryIt != m_latestVersionsByRepo.end())
+      FindAddonAndCheckForUpdate(addon, repoEntryIt->second, update);
+  }
 
   if (update)
   {
